# .env holds secrets; they are injected at run time, never baked in.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.venv
data/
docs/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
*.egg-info
# tests/ is NOT ignored: the `test` stage needs it. The runtime stage simply
# never COPYs it, so it does not reach the shipped image.
